P2 is done and ticked in `tasks.md`. Typecheck and lint are clean, and `pnpm test` passes 227/227 across 40 files. In the final full `pnpm e2e` run, 14 of 16 passed. The 2 that failed are timing tests that fail without my changes too (details at the end).

**What's in place**
- **`palette.ts`** now exports:
  - `THEME_TOKENS.light` and `THEME_TOKENS.dark`: every §3.2 colour, the materials, focus ring, selection, the §3.7 shadows, `barNeutral`, and the page bin colours.
  - `WAFER_TOKENS` (§3.3) and both bin palettes (§3.5).
  - `getBinColor(rank, 'disc' | 'light' | 'dark')`.
- **`tokens.ts`** has the premium values for:
  - radii;
  - the new 56 and 72 spacing steps and the per-breakpoint grids;
  - z-layers 35 (hints) and 55 (tooltips);
  - springs with no bounce, plus a new `sheen` spring;
  - durations `dur-0` to `dur-4`, `ease-in-out`, and press scales.
- **`globals.css`**:
  - defines the variables under `:root[data-theme="light"]` and `:root[data-theme="dark"]` and maps them in `@theme inline`;
  - makes `dark:` follow `data-theme`;
  - re-samples the CSS `spring-ui` curve so it no longer overshoots;
  - makes materials opaque under reduced transparency.
- **Tests:** the new `theme-tokens.test.ts` checks every token value and every contrast ratio in §3.2, §3.3 and §3.5. That includes `text-tertiary` at 4.5:1 or better on `bg`, `surface` and `surface-sunken` in both themes, and `pass-tile-hc` at 3.1:1 (A13). It also checks that the CSS values match `THEME_TOKENS`. A new e2e test, `theme-tokens-p2.spec.ts`, covers A1 at token level by setting `data-theme` itself and reading the computed colours.

**Decisions where premium.md is silent (all in `logs/progress.md`)**
- **The app looks the same until P3.** Nothing sets `data-theme` yet, so a small fallback block keeps the old dark text colours when the attribute is missing.
- **Radius classes were renamed so pixel sizes stay the same** (for example, the 24 px class went from `rounded-lg` to `rounded-2xl`). The one visible change is `rounded-xs`, which goes from 6 px to 4 px because premium.md has no 6 px radius.
- **The brush-rectangle animation** uses its own spring loop, so it gets a stiffness/damping version of the new snappy spring (810 / 57).
- **Some dark-theme ratios in §3.2 are lower than the real values.** For example, primary text on `surface` is stated as 15.2:1 but measures 15.96:1. The tests treat each stated ratio as a minimum.

**Things you should know**
- **Old build:** the e2e server reuses whatever is in `.next`, so my first run tested an old build. I rebuilt with `pnpm build` before the runs above. Rebuild after any CSS change, or the e2e results won't reflect it.
- **The 2 failing tests** are `perf-gate` and `linked-interactions-r7` (793 ms against a 780 ms limit). Both passed when rerun. With my changes stashed, `linked-interactions-r7` still failed 3 of 4 runs, so the flakiness predates this task.
- **Sandbox change:** Chromium couldn't start because system libraries were missing, so I installed them with apt (libatk, libatspi, libxcomposite, libxdamage).
- **Acceptance log:** I created `logs/premium-acceptance.md` with a P2 entry. It has no screenshots, because nothing looks different until P3 sets `data-theme`.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=234

